# The scenes of the mutation-testing deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# mutation-testing.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in mutation-testing.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: PIT, its support for JUnit 5, and the Gradle PIT plugin, in the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/pitest/" "gradle/libs.versions.toml" --mark 44,112

## Scene 2: step 2, PIT's own options
note "Step 2: in your own build, the Gradle PIT plugin, or PIT's Maven plugin, adds the pitest task."
note "The lesson's build has the task already. One of PIT's options chooses the weak tests or the strong tests:"
show lessons/mutation-testing/example/build.gradle.kts 11 21 "lesson build file" --zoom 12-16

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: discountPercent works out the discount, and finalPrice takes it off the total."
show DiscountCalculator 18 40 --zoom 23-25

## Scene 4: the weak tests
note "The *weak* tests. Every line of the calculator runs, so line coverage is 100%."
note "Each comment says what the test fails to check."
show DiscountCalculatorWeakTest 18 39 --zoom 26-27

## Scene 5: the weak test that checks a number is not null
note "The last *weak* test checks that the final price is not null. An int never is, so the check can't fail."
show DiscountCalculatorWeakTest 47 51 --zoom 49-50

## Scene 6: PIT on the weak tests
note "Run PIT against the *weak* tests. For every planted bug it shows which tests ran, and whether one failed."
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:mutation-testing:pitest -Pcode=today"
show DiscountCalculator 18 40 --mark 19,23,25,30,31,33,39 --zoom 25
callout "Line 25: if >= 5_000 became > 5_000, an order of exactly £50 would lose its discount, and no test checks an order of exactly £50."

## Scene 7: the strong tests
note "The *strong* tests check exact values, on both sides of every boundary."
show DiscountCalculatorStrongTest 18 40 --zoom 22-23

## Scene 8: PIT on the strong tests
note "Run PIT against the *strong* tests:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:mutation-testing:pitest"
show DiscountCalculator 18 40 --mark 19,23,25,30,31,33,39
callout "Same 100% line coverage. Only mutation testing shows which tests catch bugs."
